   103	    Move each scattered fragment group into the template hole whose area matches it.
   104	
   105	    Input structure:
   106	    - The grid has one dominant background color.
   107	    - Several large monochrome rectangles act as templates; each template encloses one connected background-colored hole.
   108	    - Outside the templates, each fragment group consists of several disconnected pieces of one shared color, and fragment colors differ from template colors.
   109	
   110	    Rule:
   111	    - Detect every template and measure the area of its internal hole.
   112	    - For each fragment color, sum the pixels across all of its scattered pieces.
   113	    - Pair fragment groups to template holes by equal total area, erase the original fragments, and fill the matched hole with that fragment color.
   114	
   115	    Key insight:
   116	    The visible output depends only on area-based pairing: because every fragment group is monochrome, any valid packing fills its matched hole as one solid same-colored region.
